		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=32523#p32523"><![CDATA[
Well, you can use GJK for closest point to triangle and warmstart with the latest simplex (again have a look at Box2D). I would be surprised if this would make a difference though. You will not get around running any of the routines you mentioned. The speed-up usually comes from calling them as seldom as possible, so if you still have performance issues I would check your culling routines.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14">Dirk Gregorius</a> — Sat Jan 04, 2014 7:49 pm</p><hr />
